# Room 3 — hidden trading defaults

If a default decides **how much money**, **when orders fire**, **flatten/kill**, or **session gates**, it must be said out loud in UI and in chat. Do not let equal-split sizing, silent 1-share fallbacks, or similar sit until the first fill.

When adding execution logic: put the rule on the execution posture / watch book, and tell the user in plain language.

**Size (current):** Trading today opens **50% 15m / 30% 5m / 20% 1m**. Those are starting reservations, not walls. Extra fills collect leftover from buckets that are not hot (live < projected). A live 15m still under half its layout move can add once from that idle cash. A hot 5m/1m keeps its pot and can pull quiet 15m leftover. Wallpaper/IDF is not in the formula yet. See `room3_matrix.size_explain()` and the Timeframe buckets table.
